      "status": "approve",
      "reasoning": "Both additions denote clarified rumen fluid. DSMZ322/213/275 explicitly prepare it by filtration, heating and centrifugation; JCM355/1201/1330 explicitly resolve the see-below pointer to heat-treated, centrifuged rumen fluid. DSMZ uses 121 C/27000 g/20 min and JCM uses 120 C/25000 g/15 min, so the common material-class label does not establish identical batches or formulations. The source-qualified see-below alias is approved only for these traced contexts. The existing MICRO grounding is unchanged and still requires its independent native/full-owner gate.",
